a request:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 13\r\n
  \r\n
  GET /hello []
two requests in one write:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 9\r\n
  \r\n
  GET /1 []HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 9\r\n
  \r\n
  GET /2 []
a length:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 20\r\n
  \r\n
  POST /upload [hello]
chunks with an extension and a trailer:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 26\r\n
  \r\n
  POST /upload [hello world]
HEAD:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 14\r\n
  \r\n
  
HTTP/1.0 without a Host:
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 11\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  GET /old []
a length and a coding:
  HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 90\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  malformed HTTP message: a request has `Transfer-Encoding` or `Content-Length`, never both

a coding that is not chunked:
  HTTP/1.1 501 Not Implemented\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 76\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  not supported: the transfer coding `gzip, chunked`: only `chunked` is built

a bare LF:
  HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 65\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  malformed HTTP message: a line ends in CR LF and in nothing else

a folded line:
  HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 85\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  malformed HTTP message: a field continues the line before it (obsolete line folding)

no Host:
  HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 67\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  malformed HTTP message: an HTTP/1.1 request has exactly one `Host`

two Hosts:
  HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 67\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  malformed HTTP message: an HTTP/1.1 request has exactly one `Host`

another version:
  HTTP/1.1 505 HTTP Version Not Supported\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 41\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  HTTP version `HTTP/2.0` is not supported

a head over its limit:
  HTTP/1.1 431 Request Header Fields Too Large\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 74\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  the head of the message is larger than 65536 bytes or has too many fields

a body cut short:
  HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n
  Content-Length: 16\r\n
  Connection: close\r\n
  \r\n
  400 Bad Request

